==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|frm|lamentable}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|lāmentābilis||full of sorrow, mournful; deplorable}}, from {{m|la|lāmentor||lament}}, from {{m|la|lāmenta||wailing, weeping}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ləˈmɛn.tə.bəl/|/ˈlæm.ən.tə.bəl/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Causing [[sorrow]], [[distress]] or [[regret]]; [[deplorable]], [[pitiful]] or [[distressing]].

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Thesaurus:lamentable]]

